# Read when the site is built (the NEXT_PUBLIC_ values are put into the page, so nothing secret goes here: a key in
# the node's address would be public).

# The deployed breaks program. Without it the "Load from the chain" part of the verify page is hidden.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_BREAKS_PROGRAM_ID=
# The deployed treasury program. Without it the Treasury page says the site is not set up to read the chain.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_TREASURY_PROGRAM_ID=
# A node that answers browsers (CORS). Default: https://api.devnet.solana.com (devnet only: CLAUDE.md, guardrails)
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SOLANA_RPC_URL=
# Where the keeper's published lists are served (its PUBLISH_DIR, over https, with CORS open to this site): the verify
# page loads a break's eligibility list and cards from there and checks them against the chain. Without it they are pasted.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_PUBLISHED_URL=
# The shape of the next break, copied from the keeper's BREAK_* settings, for the reserve bar. All four or none (prices in
# micro-USDC, so $20 is 20000000). The site cannot read these from the chain until a break exists: keep them equal to the keeper's.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_BREAK_PACKS is the keeper's BREAK_PACKS exactly as it is written there: a JSON list of groups, each a machine,
# the most one pack from it may cost and how many of the break's packs come from it (one pack per spot, so the counts add up to
# paid + free spots). Keep the single quotes. For example, for 6 paid and 2 free spots:
#   NEXT_PUBLIC_BREAK_PACKS='[{"machine":"cheap","maxPrice":"10000000","count":4},{"machine":"mid","maxPrice":"25000000","count":2},{"machine":"top","maxPrice":"50000000","count":2}]'
# NEXT_PUBLIC_BREAK_PAID_SPOTS=
# NEXT_PUBLIC_BREAK_FREE_SPOTS=
# NEXT_PUBLIC_BREAK_SPOT_PRICE=
# NEXT_PUBLIC_BREAK_PACKS=
